# Catalog refresh — always use the latest skills & agents

The tool package (`.agents/pipeline.home` → `VERSION`) is the **source of truth** for
skills, agents, rules, and pack overlays. The repo copy under `.agents/` and host
projections (`.cursor/`) must match the installed `agentic-tool` version.

## When to refresh

Refresh **before SDLC work** when any of these is true:

- `agentic-tool` was updated/reinstalled on this machine
- `agentic-tool verify` warns **catalog stale**
- `pipeline.manifest.json` → `catalog_version` ≠ `agentic-tool version`
- A skill/agent/rule you need is missing or looks outdated

## Refresh workflow (mechanical)

```bash
# 1. Update the global tool (developers — from ai-dev-pipeline repo)
pwsh ./scripts/install-local.ps1
# or: dotnet tool update -g Agentic.Tool

# 2. Refresh this repo (one command; settings-safe)
agentic-tool update
```

`update` backs up `pipeline.manifest.json` + IDE/MCP settings to `.agents/.backup/<ts>/`,
re-applies the catalog (user skills/agents/hooks/rules preserved), installs Spec Kit
integrations for every host, wires the code-search MCP (add-only), restores any user setting the
refresh changed, re-links hosts (relative symlinks into `.agents/`) and runs `verify`.

Re-detect the stack only when packs / PROJECT.md change: `/pipeline-adapt mode=update`.

**Never hand-edit** skill/rule files under `.cursor/` or `.claude/` — they are links into
`.agents/`. Catalog-owned content: edit in `core/` or packs in the tool repo. Repo-specific
additions: a new skill/agent under `.agents/` or a `## local overlay` section in an agent file.

## Coordinator / adapt rule

At session start, if `catalog_version` is behind `agentic-tool version`, **stop** and tell
the human to run `agentic-tool update` before continuing SDLC work.
